"<div class=\"wrap\"><section aria-labelledby=\"calc-h\" id=\"team-calculator\" class=\"calculator-section\">\n    <div class=\"section-heading\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">01 / Build your team</p><h2 id=\"calc-h\">Your team, at a glance</h2><p class=\"lede\">Add your team’s survey results. Explore the strengths you share and the postures worth practicing.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"calc\">\n      <div class=\"field\">\n        <label for=\"team\">Team name (optional)</label>\n        <input id=\"team\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"e.g. Product Team\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"roster-head\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Team Members</span><span class=\"hint\">Names are optional and are not saved</span></div>\n      <div class=\"roster\" id=\"roster\"></div>\n      <button class=\"btn add\" id=\"addMember\" type=\"button\">+ Add team member</button>\n      <p class=\"sec-status\" id=\"secStatus\"></p>\n      <div class=\"bar\" id=\"bar\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n      <div class=\"legend\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n        <span><i class=\"dot\" style=\"background:var(--orange)\"></i>Dreamer Persona</span>\n        <span><i class=\"dot\" style=\"background:var(--grey-mid)\"></i>Planner Persona</span>\n        <span><i class=\"dot\" style=\"background:var(--fg)\"></i>Doer Persona</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"size\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">Team Size</span><b id=\"size\">0</b></div>\n      <div class=\"sec-toggle\">\n        <div class=\"eyebrow\" id=\"calcBy\">Calculate posture from</div>\n        <div class=\"seg\" role=\"radiogroup\" aria-labelledby=\"calcBy\">\n          <button type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" id=\"modeP\" aria-checked=\"false\">Primary only</button>\n          <button type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" id=\"modePS\" aria-checked=\"true\">Primary + Secondary</button>\n        </div>\n        <small class=\"weight\" id=\"weightNote\">Each Primary Persona counts 2 points. Each Secondary Persona counts 1 point.</small>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n      <span class=\"pill\">Team Persona Posture</span>\n      <h3 id=\"summary\">Add your team's personas</h3>\n      <p id=\"desc\">Add each team member's Primary and Secondary Persona.</p>\n      <div class=\"qa\" id=\"qa\" hidden></div>\n      <div class=\"ask\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Manager asks</div><p id=\"question\">What does the work need right now?</p></div>\n      <div class=\"deep\" id=\"primDeep\" hidden></div>\n      <div class=\"deep\" id=\"secDeep\" hidden></div>\n      <div class=\"coverage\" id=\"coverage\" hidden>\n        <div class=\"eyebrow\">Posture Score Breakdown</div>\n        <p id=\"secSummary\" hidden></p>\n        <div class=\"tbl\"><table>\n          <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Persona</th><th scope=\"col\">Primary ×2</th><th scope=\"col\">Secondary ×1</th><th scope=\"col\">Posture score</th><th scope=\"col\">Top two</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody id=\"covBody\"></tbody>\n        </table></div>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"gap-note\" id=\"gapnote\" hidden></p>\n      <p class=\"note\" id=\"countnote\">Counts reflect surveyed primary preferences, not fixed abilities or current meeting posture.</p>\n      <div class=\"actions\">\n        <button class=\"btn primary\" id=\"copy\" type=\"button\">Copy Team Posture</button>\n        <button class=\"btn\" id=\"reset\" type=\"button\">Reset</button>\n        <span class=\"toast\" id=\"toast\" role=\"status\"></span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section><section aria-labelledby=\"fr-h\">\n    <h2 id=\"fr-h\">Potential Friction Points</h2>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Based on this team's persona mix. Friction is not conflict. It is a signal that the team may need to switch personas on purpose.</p>\n    <div class=\"friction\" id=\"friction\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n  </section><section aria-labelledby=\"why-h\" class=\"why\">\n    <h2 id=\"why-h\">Why this tool exists</h2>\n    <div class=\"why-grid\">\n      <article class=\"why-card\">\n        <span class=\"why-step\">The problem</span>\n        <h3>Teams stall when they think in different ways at the same moment</h3>\n        <p>Teams rarely fail for lack of talent or information. They stall when one member is in the Dreamer Persona exploring new ideas, another is in the Planner Persona locking in details, and a third is in the Doer Persona pushing to act. Without a shared language for this, it shows up as conflict, resistance, or \"poor communication,\" and innovation, collaboration, and execution all suffer.</p>\n      </article>\n      <article class=\"why-card\">\n        <span class=\"why-step\">The usual approach</span>\n        <h3>Assessments and workshops that describe people</h3>\n        <p>Most organizations reach for personality assessments such as DISC, Enneagram, CliftonStrengths, or 16 Personalities, plus team-building workshops. They build self-awareness, but they:</p>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Label each person with a fixed type</li>\n          <li>Keep the insight in individual reports</li>\n          <li>Rarely change how the team works together the next day</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n      <article class=\"why-card dpd\">\n        <span class=\"why-step\">How DPD is different</span>\n        <h3>A shared language that aligns thinking and behavior</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><b>Personas are postures, not labels.</b> Everyone can switch into the Dreamer Persona, Planner Persona, and Doer Persona.</li>\n          <li><b>The team is the unit.</b> This tool shows your team's collective persona posture, not just individual results.</li>\n          <li><b>Insight becomes action.</b> It names what the team needs to practice and which meeting mode to use.</li>\n          <li><b>It works with what you have.</b> DPD complements the assessments your team already uses.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"why-use\"><b>How to use it:</b> enter each member's Primary and Secondary Persona from DPDing, read your Team Persona Posture, then choose the meeting mode the work needs.</p>\n  </section><section aria-labelledby=\"terms-h\" class=\"terms\">\n    <h2 id=\"terms-h\">Key terms</h2>\n    <dl class=\"term-list\">\n      <div class=\"term\">\n        <dt>Persona</dt>\n        <dd>A way of thinking and working that anyone can switch into. DPD has three: the <b>Dreamer Persona</b> expands, the <b>Planner Persona</b> organizes, and the <b>Doer Persona</b> executes. A persona describes the work your mind is doing, not who you are. Your <b>Primary Persona</b> is the one you prefer. Your <b>Secondary Persona</b> is the one you reach for next.</dd>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"term\">\n        <dt>Posture</dt>\n        <dd>The persona you are using right now. Your preference is where you start. Your posture is where you are in the moment, and you can switch it on purpose. Each meeting mode asks the whole team to take the same posture at the same time.</dd>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"term\">\n        <dt>Team Persona Posture</dt>\n        <dd>The combined picture of your team's primary and secondary preferences. It shows the team's natural lean, its backup strengths, its gaps, and where friction is likely. It describes tendencies, not limits.</dd>\n      </div>\n    </dl>\n    <article class=\"example\">\n      <span class=\"why-step\">Example: a team of 5</span>\n      <div class=\"tbl\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Persona</th><th scope=\"col\">Primary</th><th scope=\"col\">Secondary</th><th scope=\"col\">Share</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Planner Persona</td><td>3</td><td>1</td><td class=\"top\">47%</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Doer Persona</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>33%</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Dreamer Persona</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>20%</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n      <p><b>What it shows:</b> a slight lean toward the Planner Persona, so planning is a strength and the team likes structure, owners, and dates. Three members hold the Doer Persona as their Secondary Persona, so execution has backup strength. The Dreamer Persona is least represented, so innovation will not happen by default. The team should schedule Dream Meeting Mode on purpose before planning starts.</p>\n      <button class=\"btn ex\" type=\"button\" data-m=\"1-0,1-2,1-2,0-2,2-1\">Load this example into the calculator</button>\n    </article>\n  </section><section aria-labelledby=\"pe-h\">\n    <h2 id=\"pe-h\">The Three Personas</h2>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Each persona is a way of working, not a type of person. Everyone can switch into any of them. These describe what each persona does well and where it can overreach.</p>\n    <div class=\"personas\" id=\"personas\"></div>\n  </section><section aria-labelledby=\"mo-h\">\n    <h2 id=\"mo-h\">The Five Meeting Modes</h2>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Name the mode before every meeting. Each mode asks the whole team to take the same persona posture, whatever their primary preference.</p>\n    <div class=\"modes\">\n      <article class=\"mode\">\n        <header><span class=\"num\">0</span><div><h3>Mind Dump</h3><span class=\"posture\">All Personas</span></div></header>\n        <p><b>Definition:</b> An open, unfiltered capture of everything on the team's mind about the work: ideas, tasks, worries, and questions.</p>\n        <p><b>Purpose:</b> Clear mental clutter so the team sees the whole picture before choosing a mode.</p>\n        <h4>Rules</h4>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Everyone contributes, from every persona.</li>\n          <li>Capture everything where the whole team can see it.</li>\n          <li>No evaluating, debating, or solving yet.</li>\n          <li>Time-box it, for example 10 minutes.</li>\n          <li>End by sorting each item into Dream, Plan, or Do.</li>\n        </ul>\n              <h4 class=\"off\">Off limits</h4>\n        <ul class=\"offl\">\n          <li>Judging, debating, or ranking what is shared</li>\n          <li>Solving problems or assigning tasks</li>\n          <li>Filtering out items that seem small or off-topic</li>\n          <li>Deciding priorities</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n      <article class=\"mode\">\n        <header><span class=\"num\">1</span><div><h3>Dream Meeting Mode</h3><span class=\"posture\">Dreamer Persona Posture</span></div></header>\n        <p><b>Definition:</b> A meeting where everyone switches into the Dreamer Persona to explore what could be.</p>\n        <p><b>Purpose:</b> Generate options and direction before narrowing down.</p>\n        <h4>Rules</h4>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Everyone switches into the Dreamer Persona.</li>\n          <li>Build on ideas with \"yes, and.\"</li>\n          <li>No judging feasibility, budget, or timelines yet.</li>\n          <li>Bold ideas are welcome. Capture every one.</li>\n          <li>End by choosing a short list to carry into Plan Meeting Mode.</li>\n        </ul>\n              <h4 class=\"off\">Off limits</h4>\n        <ul class=\"offl\">\n          <li>Feasibility checks, budgets, and timelines</li>\n          <li>Shutting ideas down with \"we tried that before\"</li>\n          <li>Assigning owners or tasks</li>\n          <li>Picking a final answer too early</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n      <article class=\"mode\">\n        <header><span class=\"num\">2</span><div><h3>Plan Meeting Mode</h3><span class=\"posture\">Planner Persona Posture</span></div></header>\n        <p><b>Definition:</b> A meeting where everyone switches into the Planner Persona to turn chosen ideas into structure.</p>\n        <p><b>Purpose:</b> Agree on what will happen, who owns it, and when.</p>\n        <h4>Rules</h4>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Everyone switches into the Planner Persona.</li>\n          <li>Work only from ideas chosen in Dream Meeting Mode. Park new ideas for the next Dream round.</li>\n          <li>Give every task one owner and a date.</li>\n          <li>Name risks and dependencies.</li>\n          <li>End with a plan everyone can state back.</li>\n        </ul>\n              <h4 class=\"off\">Off limits</h4>\n        <ul class=\"offl\">\n          <li>Brand-new ideas. Park them for the next Dream round.</li>\n          <li>Reopening ideas the team already chose</li>\n          <li>Starting the work during the meeting</li>\n          <li>Tasks without an owner or a date</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n      <article class=\"mode\">\n        <header><span class=\"num\">3</span><div><h3>Do Meeting Mode</h3><span class=\"posture\">Doer Persona Posture</span></div></header>\n        <p><b>Definition:</b> A meeting where everyone switches into the Doer Persona to move the plan forward.</p>\n        <p><b>Purpose:</b> Turn the plan into progress and clear what is blocking it.</p>\n        <h4>Rules</h4>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Everyone switches into the Doer Persona.</li>\n          <li>Share progress and blockers, not new ideas or re-planning.</li>\n          <li>Solve blockers fast or take them offline.</li>\n          <li>Keep it short.</li>\n          <li>End with next actions and owners.</li>\n        </ul>\n              <h4 class=\"off\">Off limits</h4>\n        <ul class=\"offl\">\n          <li>Brainstorming or new ideas</li>\n          <li>Re-planning scope or timelines. Flag it for Plan or Assess Meeting Mode.</li>\n          <li>Long problem-solving discussions</li>\n          <li>Updates with no next action</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n      <article class=\"mode\">\n        <header><span class=\"num\">4</span><div><h3>Assess Meeting Mode</h3><span class=\"posture\">Review</span></div></header>\n        <p><b>Definition:</b> A meeting to step back and review results and how the team used each persona posture.</p>\n        <p><b>Purpose:</b> Learn what worked and decide which mode the team needs next.</p>\n        <h4>Rules</h4>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Compare results against the plan.</li>\n          <li>Ask which persona postures helped and which were missing.</li>\n          <li>Focus on the process, not on blame.</li>\n          <li>Capture lessons where the team can find them again.</li>\n          <li>End by choosing the next mode. Often that is Mind Dump or Dream.</li>\n        </ul>\n              <h4 class=\"off\">Off limits</h4>\n        <ul class=\"offl\">\n          <li>Blame or personal critique</li>\n          <li>Redoing the work in the meeting</li>\n          <li>Planning the next round before lessons are captured</li>\n          <li>Skipping what went well</li>\n        </ul>\n      </article>\n    </div>\n  </section><section aria-labelledby=\"ex-h\">\n    <h2 id=\"ex-h\">Try an Example</h2>\n    <div class=\"examples\">\n      <button class=\"ex\" type=\"button\" data-m=\"0-2,0-2,1-0\"><b>Team of 3</b><span>Primary: Dreamer Persona 2 · Planner Persona 1 · Doer Persona 0</span><span>Secondary: Dreamer Persona 1 · Planner Persona 0 · Doer Persona 2</span></button>\n      <button class=\"ex\" type=\"button\" data-m=\"0-2,1-0,1-0,1-2,2-1\"><b>Team of 5</b><span>Primary: Dreamer Persona 1 · Planner Persona 3 · Doer Persona 1</span><span>Secondary: Dreamer Persona 2 · Planner Persona 1 · Doer Persona 2</span></button>\n      <button class=\"ex\" type=\"button\" data-m=\"0-1,0-2,1-0,1-0,2-0,2-1,2-1\"><b>Team of 7</b><span>Primary: Dreamer Persona 2 · Planner Persona 2 · Doer Persona 3</span><span>Secondary: Dreamer Persona 3 · Planner Persona 3 · Doer Persona 1</span></button>\n    </div>\n  </section><section aria-labelledby=\"sc-h\">\n    <h2 id=\"sc-h\">Manager Facilitation Script</h2>\n    <div class=\"script\">\n      <p>\"Now that we have our individual results, let's look at our team as a whole.</p>\n      <p>We have <mark id=\"sD\">0</mark> Dreamer Personas, <mark id=\"sP\">0</mark> Planner Personas, and <mark id=\"sO\">0</mark> Doer Personas represented as primary preferences.</p>\n      <p id=\"secLine\" hidden>As secondary preferences, we have <mark id=\"s2D\">0</mark> Dreamer Personas, <mark id=\"s2P\">0</mark> Planner Personas, and <mark id=\"s2O\">0</mark> Doer Personas. These are personas many of us can switch into when the work calls for them.</p>\n      <p>This gives us a snapshot of how we naturally prefer to approach work.</p>\n      <p>It doesn't mean anyone is limited to one persona. We can all Dream, Plan, and Do.</p>\n      <p>The question is: Are we using the right persona for the work we're doing at the moment?</p>\n      <p>What's one thing we could do differently in our next meeting?\"</p>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"tip\">For the first manager experience, use primary personas only. Introduce secondary personas as a second level of analysis once the team is comfortable with the language.</p>\n  </section><section class=\"cta\" aria-labelledby=\"cta-h\">\n    <div class=\"eyebrow\">Take the next step</div>\n    <h2 id=\"cta-h\">Schedule a Team Building Webinar</h2>\n    <p>Turn your Team Persona Posture into practice. A DPD facilitator walks your team through switching between the Dreamer Persona, Planner Persona, and Doer Persona, and running each meeting mode with intention.</p>\n    <a class=\"btn primary cta-btn\" href=\"/webinars\">Schedule a Team Building Webinar</a>\n    \n    \n  </section></div>"